# Every environment variable @ujira/db reads. Twelve of them: one for
# transport, four connection URLs, four pool sizes and three timeouts.
#
# Two line shapes, and a test depends on both. A plain `NAME=value` line is
# a variable with no default, so the process will not start without it. A
# `# default: NAME=value` line is a variable the package supplies itself,
# and the value shown is the real default read out of the code; uncomment
# the line only to change it.
#
# The test lives in src/env-template.test.ts. It fails if a variable is
# added to the package and not to this file, if a variable is listed here
# that nothing in the package reads, if a default printed here stops
# matching the default in the code, or if the placeholder values below stop
# forming a configuration the loader accepts. A template nobody checks
# becomes a document that describes a system that has moved on.
#
# Passwords never belong in this file. Fill them from the secret manager at
# deploy time; REPLACE_ME is a placeholder, not a value.

# How the connection to the server is protected.
#
# `pinned`, the default, verifies the server against the one certificate
# embedded in src/tls.ts. Nothing else is trusted: not the system trust
# store, not a certificate the URL names, and the URL may not carry an
# ssl parameter at all, because that would replace or disable the pin.
#
# `off` connects with no TLS, and it refuses to do so for anything but a
# loopback host: localhost, 127.0.0.1 or ::1. Point any URL at a real host
# with this set and the process stops at startup rather than sending
# tenant identifiers and payout rows across a network in the clear. It
# exists for a local container and a developer's own Postgres, and it has
# no use in a deployed environment.
# default: UJIRA_DB_TLS=pinned

# The four logins, one per role, each with its own pool. Get these from the
# Supabase project's connection settings. Wrong value: the process stops at
# startup, or connects as a role with the wrong grants.
#
# Port matters. 6543 is the transaction pooler and 5432 is the session
# pooler. The worker and the migrator are refused on 6543: the transaction
# pooler delivers no LISTEN notification, so the worker would wait forever,
# and the migration tool holds its advisory lock in the session, so a
# migration would lose the lock between statements.
UJIRA_DB_APP_URL=postgresql://ujira_app:REPLACE_ME@aws-0-eu-west-2.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
UJIRA_DB_WORKER_URL=postgresql://ujira_worker:REPLACE_ME@aws-0-eu-west-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
UJIRA_DB_READER_URL=postgresql://ujira_reader:REPLACE_ME@aws-0-eu-west-2.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
UJIRA_DB_MIGRATION_URL=postgresql://ujira_migrator:REPLACE_ME@aws-0-eu-west-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Connections per process, per role. The database allows 60 in total and
# this deployment may use 30 of them, so the four numbers are checked
# against that sum and startup fails if they exceed it. Render runs several
# instances, so raising a number here multiplies by the instance count.
# Too high and a deploy exhausts the database for everything else,
# including the dashboard and anyone holding a psql session; too low and
# requests queue behind the acquire timeout below.
# default: UJIRA_DB_APP_POOL_SIZE=8
# default: UJIRA_DB_WORKER_POOL_SIZE=4
# default: UJIRA_DB_READER_POOL_SIZE=4
# default: UJIRA_DB_MIGRATION_POOL_SIZE=1

# How long a caller waits for a free connection from the pool before it is
# given an error. Too high and a database stall turns into a queue of held
# requests; too low and an ordinary traffic peak fails requests that would
# have been served.
# default: UJIRA_DB_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# Server side limits sent on every transaction. Both must stay under the
# pooler's own 8000 ms, and startup fails if either reaches it, because a
# limit above the pooler's is never the one that fires and the error you
# get back is the pooler's rather than ours. Too low and a legitimate
# report or a large payout batch is cut off mid transaction.
# default: UJIRA_DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# default: UJIRA_DB_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS=3000
